\chapter{Additional Content}
\label{app:other}

\section{Background Dataset}
\label{sec:phase1-data}

The analysis in this thesis focuses exclusively on the analysis of Phase-II data
that is measured with AugerPrime electronics. In some instances, a verification,
especially of \UUB-reconstructed simulated air showers, is needed.

Prior validation studies have shown that there exist no systematic differences 
between Phase-I and Phase-II data, both in reconstructed station-level 
observables (Ref.~\todo{ref}), as well as event-level observables (Ref.~\todo{ref}). The Phase-I dataset, representing a large catalog of observed \CR events 
measured with \UB electronics is thus an excellent candidate to verify some 
simulation driven variables using measured data.


